## Best Practices

> **Never delete the following directories on a Linux system:**

* `/lib`
* `/lib64`
* `/usr/lib`
* `/usr/lib64`

These directories contain the shared libraries required for the Linux kernel, system binaries, package management tools, services, and user 
applications. Accidental deletion can leave the operating system unbootable and may require extensive manual recovery.
